---
import InfoPage from '../marketing/InfoPage.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL } from '../marketing/product';

const description = 'How Print Map Studio handles local project data, imported files, analytics, map service requests, browser storage, and client-side exports.';
---

<InfoPage
  title="Privacy"
  description={description}
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  heading="What stays on your device and what leaves it."
  updated="August 31, 2026"
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    Print Map Studio has no user accounts or server-side project database. Your project, imported files, and exports stay on your device. Analytics, map tiles, and optional location features send limited request data to third-party services.
  </p>

  <h2>Project data stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    The current project autosaves to IndexedDB storage associated with this site. The saved record can include your page settings, map position, styles, routes, places, shapes, and imported geographic data. Small interface preferences may be stored in localStorage, and a temporary startup-recovery flag may be stored in sessionStorage.
  </p>
  <p>
    Browser storage remains on your device until you clear site data or remove the saved project. Download a project file before clearing browser data if you need a backup.
  </p>

  <h2>Imported files and exports</h2>
  <p>
    GPX, KML, and GeoJSON files are parsed locally in your browser. Map exports, including PNG, PDF, layered SVG, and layered PSD, are generated in the browser and downloaded to your device. Print Map Studio does not upload those source files or finished exports to its own server.
  </p>

  <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Production pages load Google Analytics to understand page visits and general engagement. Google may process information such as your device and browser, approximate location, referring page, and interactions with the site, and may use cookies or similar identifiers. Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and use your browser settings or privacy tools to control cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>Map and elevation services</h2>
  <h3>OpenFreeMap</h3>
  <p>
    The editor requests map tiles, fonts, and sprites from OpenFreeMap. Those requests include your IP address, browser request metadata, and the tile coordinates needed to display the map.
  </p>
  <h3>Mapbox</h3>
  <p>
    Place search, road routing, map matching, and travel-time areas send the relevant search text or geographic coordinates to Mapbox when those features are available and you use them. Review <a href="https://www.mapbox.com/legal/privacy">Mapbox's Privacy Policy</a> for its handling of those requests.
  </p>
  <h3>Open-Meteo</h3>
  <p>
    When you request an elevation profile, sampled route coordinates are sent to the Open-Meteo elevation API. Review <a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/terms">Open-Meteo's terms and privacy information</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The public site is hosted with GitHub Pages. GitHub may process standard web request and security logs as the hosting provider. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    For a privacy question or correction, <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/issues`}>open an issue in the project repository</a>. Do not include private project data, access tokens, or other sensitive information in a public issue.
  </p>
</InfoPage>
